 4. The incredible shrinking Labubu 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Joe Raedle/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Labubu craze has faded.

 The maker, Pop Mart International, said in a preliminary sales report today that it expects its Q3 revenue to decline by 45%–50%, compared with a year earlier. Flashback: The mischievous, spiky-eared, snaggle-toothed Labubu plush dolls were the hot toy of 2025 , driving an enormous revenue increase for Pop Mart.

 A year ago, the company's revenue was soaring by 250%. Zoom in: The decline in interest appears to be particularly sharp in the Americas, where Pop Mart's sales are expected to fall by 70%–75% in the third quarter.

 💭 Nathan's thought bubble: Sounds like the Beanie Babies boom-bust all over again.

 
 
